Package: libstereo-policy1
Architecture: any
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.stereo-layer.av>
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Shared stereo policy for programs without Qt
 How a stereo mark reads (the Stereo3DLayout words of RFC 9559 StereoMode and
 H.264/H.265 Table D-8; H.264 V15, 08/2024 numbers it D-8, V16, 06/2026 D-9),
 which packing a video frame holds, whether its views are full or half, and
 the user's correction, as a small C library a browser or a player can load. libstereo-layer builds on it, so every program
 decides alike.
 .
 Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's edition of SparkyLinux (by Paweł "pavroo"
 Pijanowski).

