Package: libstereo-dibr1
Architecture: any
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.stereo-layer.av>
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Depth-image-based rendering for programs without Qt
 A picture and its depth map become the two views of full side by side: the
 depth conventions of H.265 and H.264 (inverse Z, disparity, Z, non-linear
 disparity), Google's Dynamic Depth ranges, depth sensors' distances, the
 depth and parallax maps of ISO/IEC 23002-3 and plain 2D-plus-depth; the
 picture as the left eye or the middle; forward, backward or layered warping;
 background extension, depth-aided or Telea hole filling; optional asymmetric
 smoothing of the depth; a second layer, the background a picture hides or
 graphics over it. The same core runs as GLSL passes in a program's own
 OpenGL or OpenGL ES context. One core for FFmpeg's dibr filter, players and
 the desktop, so they all draw the same views.
 .
 Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's edition of SparkyLinux (by Paweł "pavroo"
 Pijanowski).

